# Copy to .env.test and fill in a TEMPORARY development/test database — never point this at
# staging or production. Loaded by `npm run test:integration` / `test:e2e` / `db:migrate:test` /
# `db:seed:test` via dotenv-cli, so those commands never touch whatever DATABASE_URL is set to
# in your shell or in apps/api/.env (the local-dev database).

# A database dedicated to test runs. Test suites truncate their own seeded rows on teardown
# (see afterAll() in each *.e2e-spec.ts) but should never share a database with local dev data.
#
# If your test Postgres sits behind a plaintext-only TCP proxy (observed with a Railway-hosted
# instance during Phase 6A verification), Prisma's query engine's default SSL negotiation attempt
# fails with P1001 even though a plain `pg` client connects fine — append `?sslmode=disable` to
# both URLs below in that case. Do not use sslmode=disable for anything that isn't a disposable
# test database.
DATABASE_URL=
DIRECT_URL=
REDIS_URL=

NODE_ENV=test
JWT_ACCESS_SECRET=test-access-secret-not-for-production
JWT_REFRESH_SECRET=test-refresh-secret-not-for-production
